  icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 57a8e05a8a1d4451e9081ab70ab1f576, type: 3}
  itemDescription: Microelectronics and Semiconductors Technologies Institute  This
    institute leads R&D in microelectronics and semiconductor technologies. Its mission
    is to build domestic capability in chip design and fabrication, supporting everything
    from integrated circuits for sensors to power electronics and emerging fields
    like MEMS (micro-electromechanical systems). Key focus areas include semiconductor
    device design, process development for fabrication (cleanroom processes, lithography),
    and establishing pilot production lines for specialized chips (e.g. for communications
    or defense). The institute also handles research in nanofabrication and electronics
    packaging. By advancing these technologies, it supports initiatives like the
    Saudi Semiconductor Program launched in 2024 to localize chip design and talent.
    Ultimately, it strives to reduce reliance on imports and foster a local semiconductor
    ecosystem
  description: 
